  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x|+a$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units up.\n\nHere, the graph is moved down by $8$ units. This corresponds to $a=-8.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the curve is $y=|x|-8.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/477932b4bf3420b86a105da3ffe8c554ff9778fe574d62ef4625a29834b2ec83.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
